    "q-40836": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40836",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Q$ shown above. Find the matrix $R$ such that $A=QR$ is a QR factorization of $A.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $Q$ has orthonormal columns, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}^{T}\\cdot A & ={Q}^{T}\\cdot QR \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & =({Q}^{T}\\,Q)R \\\\ {Q}^{T}\\,A & ={I}_{2}R \\\\ R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that ${Q}^{T}Q={I}_{2}$ since the columns of $Q$ are orthonormal.\n\nNow, we calculate the matrix $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-40836-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "R=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3} & \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]",
