      "source_example_id": "e-8324",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Triangular Factor of a QR Factorization Given the Orthogonal Factor",
      "kp_id": "e-8324"
    },
    "q-41484": {
      "dom_id": "step-q41484",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{2}+6{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-2{q}_{1}+{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{23}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{2}+6{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-2{q}_{1}+{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=-30{q}_{1}+5{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}=8{q}_{1}-4{q}_{2}+4{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -30 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{11}+{r}_{13}+{r}_{23}=3+8+(-4)=7.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
