columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\"><mtr><mtd><mstyle mathbackground=\"lightgray\"><mpadded height=\"+2pt\" depth=\"+2pt\" lspace=\"2pt\" width=\"+4pt\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></mpadded></mstyle></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>12</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>22</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">]</mo></mrow><mo>⏞</mo></mover></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathsize=\"1.44em\"><mi>R</mi></mstyle></mrow></mover><mo>.</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Consider the QR factorization of the matrix <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"442\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> shown above. Given that the columns <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"443\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msub><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D41A TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-script></mjx-msub><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-msub space=\"2\"><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-b\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D41A TEX-B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\