    "q-40838": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40838",
      "name": "Question 24",
      "problem": "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained from the columns of $A$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, find  the value of ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{12}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ be the columns of $A.$\n\nFirst, we find an orthonormal basis of $\\text{Col}(A)=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process.\n\n**Step 1**. We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**. We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-(-\\frac{12}{6})[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we normalize ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{12}=(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})\\cdot (-2\\sqrt{6})=2\\sqrt{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
